  "description": "The Crew Mini is all about wheelies, laughs, and the kind of mini bike fun that makes you say “just one more lap” about ten times. Inspired by classic pit bikes with a little BMX attitude mixed in, it delivers that playful, throttle-happy ride feel in a compact electric package that’s easy to control and dangerously hard to put away. The 20” wheels give it a more planted, confidence-inspiring ride than traditional pit bikes, while still keeping the lightweight, tossable character that makes mini bikes so addictive.\nA 500W hub motor paired with a 48V 10Ah lithium-ion battery provides quick acceleration and plenty of punch for neighborhood cruising, pit sessions, and general goofing around. Mechanical disc brakes keep things simple, durable, and easy to maintain while delivering reliable stopping power. The Crew Mini isn’t about chasing top speed — it’s about smiles per mile, spontaneous wheelies, and finding new excuses to ride when you definitely have other things you should be doing.\nThe Crew Mini is classified as a motorized scooter under California Vehicle Code. A “motorized scooter” is defined as a two wheeled device with handlebars, powered by an electric motor, and equipped with either a floorboard designed for standing or a seat with footrests. The Crew Mini falls within this classification and is not considered a motorcycle, moped, or motor driven cycle under California law.",
